notes.body:
There is no requirement for Wireshark to, for `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN` packets, include the metadata in SocketCAN format. It could, for example, define a pseudo-header structure for CAN packets in wiretap/wtap.h - one that could include metadata that the SocketCAN header defined by Linux doesn't support - and:

* in code that reads `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN` from pcap and pcapng files, fill in the pseudo-header appropriately;
* in code that writes `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN` to pcap and pcapng files, construct the SocketCAN pseudo-header based on the pseudo-header;
* do similar things for `LINKTYPE_LINUX_SLL` and `LINKTYPE_LINUX_SLL2` captures;
* do similar things for other file formats.

See:

* the definition of `union wtap_pseudo_header`, and the definition of the types of the members of that union, in wiretap/wtap.h;
* the `pcap_read_XXX_pseudoheader()` and `pcap_write_XXX_pseudoheader()` routines, and the places where they're called, in wiretap/pcap-common.c.

